7 deletions(-) [owned-diff-check] should be empty. Existing unrelated worktree changes are recorded, not changed or “cleaned up.” A mismatch in branch, count, uniqueness, or package shortstat becomes SCOPE-DRIFT-02 in 05-proof-gaps.md; stop before substantive findings and hand the mismatch to the manager. 4. Exact lane artifact structure Create only: .notes/oracle/branch-trust-audit/lanes/02-core-surfaces/ ├── 00-scope.tsv ├── 00-owned-paths.txt ├── 01-inventory.tsv ├── 02-change-map.md ├── 03-observed-improvements.md ├── 04-breakage-candidates.md ├── 05-proof-gaps.md ├── 06-verification-results.md ├── 07-screenshot-requests.md ├── 08-article-integration.md ├── 09-prioritized-next-actions.md ├── 10-worker-report.md ├── run-receipt.py └── receipts/ ├── 00-baseline.txt ├── 00-name-status.txt ├── 00-numstat.tsv ├── 00-function-index.txt ├── 00-source-audit-sites.txt ├── 00-added-shortcuts.txt ├── W01.diff ├── … ├── W11.diff ├── test-*.log └── runtime-*.jsonl 01-inventory.tsv Header: path group change_status added deleted changed_symbols review_state verdict confidence finding_ids evidence Allowed review_state values: UNREAD DIFFED TRACED PROVED ACCOUNTED_UNVERIFIED Generate the raw inputs: Bashxargs git diff --find-renames --name-status main...HEAD -- \ < "$LANE/00-owned-paths.txt" \ > "$LANE/receipts/00-name-status.txt" xargs git diff --find-renames --numstat main...HEAD -- \ < "$LANE/00-owned-paths.txt" \ > "$LANE/receipts/00-numstat.tsv" xargs git diff --find-renames --function-context main...HEAD -- \ < "$LANE/00-owned-paths.txt" \ | rg '^@@|^[+-]\s*(pub(\([^)]*\))?\s+)?(async\s+)?(fn|struct|enum|trait|impl)\b' \ > "$LANE/receipts/00-function-index.txt" || true Each path must end with a nonempty verdict, confidence, and evidence field. A test-only path can be PROOF_DEBT, NO_MATERIAL_CHANGE, or evidence for another finding; it cannot be silently marked “covered” because it compiled. Finding file schemas Every entry in 03-observed-improvements.md: Markdown## IMP-02-NNN — <specific title> - Verdict: - Confidence: - Risk reduced: - Owned path(s): - Exact symbol(s): - `main` behavior/structure: - Branch behavior/structure: - Concrete user-visible effect: - Falsifier: - Evidence receipts: - Counterevidence checked: - Screenshot target: - Article-ready sentence: Every entry in 04-breakage-candidates.md: Markdown## REG-02-NNN — <specific title> - Verdict: - Confidence: - Severity / likelihood: - Exact path and symbol: - Triggering input/state: - Expected output/state: - Observed or predicted wrong output/state: - Why `main` differs or why contract is violated: - Reproduction command/sequence: - Evidence receipts: - Missing proof: - Conditional future remediation: Every entry in 05-proof-gaps.md: Markdown## GAP-02-NNN — <claim that is not established> - Claim source: - Claim text, paraphrased: - Path/test/comment/receipt: - Existing evidence: - Missing boundary: - Smallest falsifier: - Final status: UNVERIFIED | CONTRADICTED | SUPERSEDED 06-verification-results.md Use one row per invocation: id | command | timeout | first result | diagnosis | rerun result | interpretation | receipt Never overwrite a failing first log with the rerun log. 5. Shared audit method for every work package For each WNN: BashGROUP=W01 # change per package awk -F '\t' -v g="$GROUP" 'NR > 1 && $2 == g { print $1 }' \ "$LANE/00-scope.tsv" \ > "$LANE/receipts/$GROUP-paths.txt" xargs git diff --find-renames --function-context main...HEAD -- \ < "$LANE/receipts/$GROUP-paths.txt" \ > "$LANE/receipts/$GROUP.diff" xargs git log --no-merges \ --format='%H%x09%ad%x09%s' --date=iso-strict main..HEAD -- \ < "$LANE/receipts/$GROUP-paths.txt" \ > "$LANE/receipts/$GROUP-commits.tsv" Then process by subsystem, not line count: List every changed symbol from the function-context diff. Identify the owning model/descriptor and every renderer or handler consuming it. Compare advertised title, shortcut, enabled state, disabled reason, destination, close policy, and return route. Trace at least one input edge and one output edge for each material symbol. Separate test-only claims from production behavior. Record one inventory row per path before moving on. Promote a claim above R2 only after the corresponding behavior or runtime proof. Cross-cutting scans: Bash# New or changed shortcut advertisements and handlers. xargs git diff -U0 main...HEAD -- < "$LANE/00-owned-paths.txt" \ | rg '^\+.*(with_shortcut|FooterButtonConfig::new|KeyBinding::new|canonical_shortcut|is_key_|⌘|⇧|⌥|⌃|Esc|Enter)' \ > "$LANE/receipts/00-added-shortcuts.txt" || true # Source-audit sites inside owned paths. xargs rg -n \ 'read_to_string\s*\(|include_str!\s*\(|include_bytes!\s*\(' \ < "$LANE/00-owned-paths.txt" \ > "$LANE/receipts/00-source-audit-sites.txt" || true # Added local visual values or timing that may bypass shared owners. xargs git diff -U0 main...HEAD -- < "$LANE/00-owned-paths.txt" \ | rg '^\+.*(px\(|rgb\(|rgba\(|hsla|Duration::from_|font_|rounded|opacity|blur|inset|padding|margin)' \ > "$LANE/receipts/00-local-visual-values.txt" || true The visual-value scan is a review queue, not an automatic defect list. 6. Ordered work packages W01 — Actions models, builders, dialog, and detached window 26 paths. Highest initial risk. Primary anchors: ActionsDialog, ActionsDialogConfig, ActionsDialogRoute activate_selected, activate_action_id, handle_escape opening_shell_sizing_snapshot, attach_to_fixed_shell, release_fixed_shell actions_window_key_intent ActionsWindow::handle_key_event sync_displayed_action_shortcut_keybindings request_close, open_actions_window, close_actions_window matching_action_id_for_canonical_shortcut get_notes_command_bar_actions Agent Chat, Notes, script-context, built-in, Flow, dictation-history, clipboard, file-search, favorites, and theme action builders Required review: Build a row-level action matrix with: host | action_id | title | section | badge | enabled rule | disabled reason handler | close policy | return focus | Agent handoff eligibility Compare main and branch for every changed builder. A renamed title or badge is behavioral because menu discovery and shortcut ownership depend on those literals. Trace detached-window keyboard routing separately from parent-window routing. Confirm hidden/disabled actions cannot execute through: Enter displayed shortcut direct automation action ID pointer activation Confirm nested route Escape pops one route before closing. Confirm search editing, Unicode cursor movement, undo/redo, filter refresh, selection identity, and fixed-shell sizing. Confirm close restores the correct parent—Main, Notes, or another supported parent—and removes all automation/runtime handles. Compare all new source-reading tests with nearby behavior tests. Record redundancy as PROOF_DEBT. Concrete failure scenarios: IDInput/stateWrong result to detectA-01Parent loses key status between popup creation and its deferred focus requestPopup closes on its first render before search receives focus.A-02Selected action is disabled; press its advertised shortcut or invoke action ID directlyCallback executes despite disabled reason.A-03Filter removes an action after its shortcut binding was registeredStale shortcut activates a hidden or now-unavailable action.A-04Child route open; press EscEntire popup closes instead of returning to root route, or stale child search remains.A-05Close with Esc/Cmd+K from Notes-hosted ActionsMain gains focus instead of Notes, or Notes editor focus is lost.A-06Actions opened with no selectable rowEnter/Cmd+Enter executes or stages a phantom/default row.A-07Cmd+Enter on deliberate selected actionWrong target, implicit launcher row, or auto-submission appears in Agent Chat.A-08Search query changes row orderPrevious index, rather than action identity or first scored row, is activated.A-09Popup opens near display edge or detached footerBounds overlap footer, use wrong display, or drift from the requested anchor.A-10Rapid open/close/openStale singleton handle prevents reopening or leaves an orphan automation window. The Actions implementation already records parent identity, fixed-shell basis, geometry, and automation generation, so runtime proof should assert those structured values rather than eyeballing placement. Focused checks: Bash./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib dialog_runtime_path_tests ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib actions::window ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib actions::builders::notes::tests ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib flow_desk_create_discoverability_tests ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib dictation_history_action_model_tests Inspect these exact tests for evidentiary quality, not only pass/fail: disabled_action_blocks_selected_and_direct_activation_without_callback ux13_opening_shell_uses_root_unfiltered_actions_through_filter_and_routes actions_search_edits_use_input_state_cursor_selection_and_history every_advertised_session_shortcut_has_a_declared_owner flow_sessions_start_a_new_conversation_the_same_way_agent_chat_does new_conversation_is_visible_but_disabled_while_a_turn_is_running Two source-audit candidates are already visible: test_actions_dialog_source_defaults_to_matching_main_window_background duplicates a behavior test by looking for an exact source string. attachment-0001-d52ae5588439a92… test_render_builtins_actions_clipboard_popup_uses_mini_menu_contract inspects formatted implementation text rather than a typed config value. Do not count these as runtime proof. W02 — Agent Chat entry, explicit context, Notes handoff, and attachment portal 7 paths. Highest protocol-truth risk. Primary anchors: AgentChatEntryRequest AgentChatEntryIntent AgentChatThreadTarget AgentChatContextPolicy AgentChatEntryOutcome AgentChatEntryDispatch resolved_agent_chat_entry_outcome pending_agent_chat_entry_dispatch dispatch_agent_chat_entry_request open_tab_ai_agent_chat_for_notes_handoff stage_notes_handoff_supplements focused-text entry and attachment-portal state transitions Required matrix: origin | intent | target host | fresh/reuse | seed text | submits? implicit focused context allowed? | explicit parts | return route source-consumed rule | completion evidence Cover at least: launcher standard open clean/quick question Quick AI with and without query selected-row Cmd+Enter detached Actions Cmd+Enter Notes primary handoff with supplements dictation send to current and fresh thread focused-text mini attachment portal active save-offer overlay active duplicate context item provider setup/error state reused thread with an existing draft The quick-question contract explicitly forbids implicit context; deliberate selection is the only launcher case that may stage the selected row. attachment-0001-d52ae5588439a92… Concrete failure scenarios: IDInput/stateWrong result to detectAI-01Fresh launcher has a default selected row; invoke quick questionA context chip or @cmd: seed is inherited.AI-02Deliberate row selected; invoke Cmd+Enter with otherwise empty launcher inputContext is suppressed even though the user deliberately targeted the row.AI-03Reuse a thread and stage a context item already presentChip count stays constant and completion is falsely reported as context_not_staged or times out.AI-04Reused thread receives an unrelated message while an entry request is pendingMessage-count increase falsely marks this request Accepted.AI-05Submission is accepted but UI message count updates after five secondsSuccessful Ask/Send is logged as entry_timeout.AI-06Notes handoff enters an existing standard full session with a draftDraft or prior messages are cleared.AI-07Notes handoff while attachment portal/save offer is activePartial context is consumed or Notes closes despite a failed handoff.AI-08Notes window invokes Ask AI while detached Agent Chat existsDetached chat is reused despite the Notes contract requiring the main host.AI-09Quick AI handoffResult auto-submits or ambient context is inherited instead of creating a fresh composer-only thread.AI-10Return from Agent Chat after Notes handoffRoute goes to launcher rather than the original Notes snapshot. Static proof gap to record immediately: current completion observation infers submission from message-count growth and context staging from context-chip-count growth. That cannot correlate the observed mutation with the initiating request and cannot distinguish duplicate context from failure. attachment-0001-d52ae5588439a92… Focused checks: Bash./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib quick_question_contract ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib agent_chat_ui_variant_launch_suppresses_selected_launcher_row_context_contract ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib dictation_send_freezes_existing_or_fresh_thread_policy These establish constructor policy only. The completion and Notes-preservation claims remain UNPROVEN_CLAIM until a live GPUI/automation sequence crosses the actual entry boundary. W03 — Launcher state, filtering, selection, navigation, native footer, sizing, and lifecycle 21 paths. Primary anchors: main_window_footer_config_with_cx main_window_footer_buttons_for_current_view dispatch_main_window_footer_shortcut dispatch_main_window_footer_action main_window_primary_action_label actions_toggle_dead_without_selection_reason set_main_window_mode calculate_window_size_params_with_app update_window_size_deferred calculate_window_size_params_if_current_view context-zone and semantic-chip dispatch filter queue/update generation selection fallback and result grouping startup navigation route lifecycle reset and window visibility Create a footer/keyboard parity ledger: surface | visible badge | canonical shortcut | enabled predicate keyboard handler | footer click handler | close/back semantics | proof At minimum include: Script List Clipboard Dictation History standalone and portal Notes Browse standalone and portal Agent Chat idle/streaming/hidden controls Flow Desk flow/session/run Form, Template, Editor, Select, Drop, Path, Env, Term Quick Terminal Confirm About Permissions SDK Reference Script Templates Theme Designer Day Page preview Kit Store/Migrate/Tips Concrete failure scenarios: IDInput/stateWrong result to detectL-01Agent Chat reports footer controls hiddenEmpty native footer band or spacer remains despite no controls, unless this is an explicitly documented geometry contract.L-02Footer advertises ⌘↵ SubmitKeyboard path does nothing, inserts a newline, or submits a different surface action.L-03Actions popup open; click non-Actions footer controlAction fires behind popup without closing it, or closes popup but drops the requested action.L-04Confirmation window activeBackground footer button remains enabled and mutates the underlying view.L-05Filter result generation returns after the view changedStale results replace the active surface or stale resize changes its bounds.L-06Selection disappears during async refreshFooter label or Enter action describes/executes the previous row.L-07Mini/full mode toggled while Actions is openOrphan popup, wrong width, stale footer, or focus loss.L-08Empty subsearch or syntax picker owns Enter/TabMain execution path bypasses picker ownership.L-09Context-zone chip is disabledPointer or keyboard still opens selector/surface.L-10Clipboard/Emoji/Dictation has no selected itemFooter says Paste/Attach rather than a disabled or neutral action. Specific static candidate: main_window_footer_chrome_should_render currently returns true for every input, including Agent Chat with controls_visible == Some(false). Both native config and GPUI footer-slot decisions use that predicate. Treat this as PLAUSIBLE_REGRESSION R1 until the actual hidden-controls state is rendered and measured. attachment-0001-d52ae5588439a92… +1 Focused checks: Bash./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib app_impl::ui_window::tests ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib shortcuts::hotkey_compat ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib scripts::tests::chunk_12 Also compare all footer badge strings with simulate_key_dispatch.rs and surface-local keyboard resolvers. A matching string in two files is not proof that the same action executes. W04 — App action dispatch and built-in execution 11 paths. Primary anchors: dispatch_actions_toggle_for_current_view actions_support_for_view Actions activation callbacks root unified result actions built-in execution match arms dictation-history action execution prompt AI actions chat actions simulated key dispatch startup-created action registrations Required analysis: For every action ID added or changed in W01, identify exactly one execution owner in W04 or its declared subsystem. Produce: action_id | builder path | handler path/symbol | input payload side effect | close policy | failure feedback | tested? Detect: advertised IDs with no handler handlers with no discoverable action multiple handlers for one ID wildcard/default arms hiding unknown IDs side effects occurring before validation ignored process-launch errors portal-sensitive actions available in the wrong mode Trace built-in navigation through startup route registration and footer/keyboard dispatch. Compare runtime_stdin or automation execution with direct UI execution for semantic parity. Concrete failure scenarios: Dictation History in attachment mode exposes Paste or Add to Agent Chat. Delete acts immediately rather than through confirmation. Built-in row says “Open” but handler clears, requests permission, or resets state. Action activation closes the popup before capturing its selected payload. Unknown action ID is silently ignored with no structured warning. File/clipboard action acts on the row now selected rather than the row captured when the popup opened. App launch/open/reveal subprocess failure produces a success HUD or no failure receipt. Footer and keyboard route to different execution branches. The output of this package is the canonical action-ID parity table in 02-change-map.md, not another production registry. W05 — Chat prompt behavior, streaming, conversation actions, and rendering 10 paths. Primary anchors: resolve_chat_render_plan resolve_chat_input_key_action_with_commands ChatPromptPreparedRequest stop/retry/recovery/dismiss request types ConversationTurnRenderKey build_conversation_turns streaming update and reveal handling turn rendering and shared conversation actions scroll follow/jump-to-latest creation feedback Concrete failure scenarios: IDInput/stateWrong result to detectC-01Assistant reply arrives for an existing user messageRender identity changes, causing selection/copy state or scroll anchoring to reset.C-02User has selected text and presses plain Cmd+CChat-level shortcut intercepts it instead of native selection copy.C-03Response streaming; press Cmd+W/EscWork is abandoned, reported as error, or dismissed without the required stop acknowledgement.C-04Response streaming; press StopTerminal state becomes failure rather than cancellation.C-05Failed turn exposes Retry without callback/capabilityEnabled action does nothing or loses original prepared request.C-06User scrolls upward during streamingAuto-follow drags them back to the bottom.C-07User returns to bottomAuto-follow remains stuck in manual mode.C-08Transcript-only hostInput, footer, focus handlers, or lifecycle ownership is accidentally installed.C-09Script-generation response already contains a fenceA second TypeScript fence is added.C-10Provider list unavailable or staleHard-coded fallback model becomes selectable but cannot execute. Focused checks: Bash./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib prompts::chat ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib conversation_turn_render_key_tests Inspect these exact tests: test_conversation_and_host_key_mappings_remain_distinct disabled_command_w_still_routes_to_safe_dismiss_acknowledgement builder_keeps_the_turn_key_stable_when_the_assistant_reply_arrives scroll-follow state tests The stable originating-message render key is a credible structural improvement, but select