and a test freezes that universal wording. attachment-0001-d52ae5588439a92… +1 Reproduce with these rows: Clear Suggested Items Check Permissions Request Accessibility Access Reset Window Positions Wrong result: Visible/native/AX primary action says “Open” while the actual operation clears, checks, requests, or resets. That is PLAUSIBLE_REGRESSION R2 from the current typed descriptor and becomes REPRODUCED_REGRESSION R4 when the branch UI and automation projection show the misleading verb. Focused checks: Bash./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib settings_hub_contract_behavior ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib flow_desk_create_discoverability_tests Do not accept every_settings_action_primary_verb_is_open as evidence of correctness; it may merely lock in the defect. W07 — Runtime stdin, prompt routing, and startup protocol 9 paths. Primary review: command deserialization and validation runtime stdin match arms duplicated or generated match-tail relationship prompt message route ownership startup registration order unknown command behavior malformed/late message handling prompt close/cancel semantics Concrete failure scenarios: Valid command handled in runtime_stdin.rs but absent from runtime_stdin_match_tail.rs, or vice versa. Malformed command partially mutates state before error return. Unknown command falls into a broad wildcard and appears successful. Late prompt message targets a replaced prompt entity. startup accepts an action before the corresponding view/handler is registered. same protocol command has different behavior through stdin and direct app dispatch. cancel/close is converted to a successful empty submission. Required output: an exhaustive command-route table with one owner per command variant. Prefer exhaustive enum matching or behavior tests over source-count assertions. W08 — Brain substrate and Day Page routing 8 paths. Primary anchors: Day Page action descriptors and execution Notes/Agent context round trip Markdown reference parsing switcher selection and return route spine integration substrate path and mutation boundaries Concrete failure scenarios: Day Page Agent action stages stale preview context after the preview closes. Agent Chat return lands on Script List rather than the original Day Page state. duplicate context is added on round trip. relative Markdown reference resolves outside the intended Brain root. day-note and normal-note identity collide. switcher selection opens Notes Window when local Day Page edit is required. stale deferred callback overwrites a newly selected day. Brain write/read claim is tested only through an in-memory helper rather than the substrate boundary. Any filesystem mutation test must use a temporary directory and must not touch the user’s actual Brain. W09 — Select, Arg, Mini, Path, and other prompts 8 paths. Trace each prompt’s: visible badge → key resolver → validation → submit callback cancel/back route → focus owner → sizing mode Concrete failure scenarios: Select with zero selections advertises enabled Run. Multiple-select prompt submits when its minimum selection contract is unmet. Drop/Path prompt submits empty data. Mini prompt consumes a key intended for its input. footer says Enter while only Cmd+Enter is handled, or the reverse. Esc cancels the script in one path but only closes UI in another. validation HUD appears but submission still proceeds. prompt mode resize uses stale item count after filter change. Focused check: Bash./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib prompts::select W10 — General built-ins 18 paths. Audit every built-in against one shared anatomy: main input/search behavior row and section owner selection reconciliation count label empty/loading/error/stale state pointer and keyboard parity native/GPUI footer parity Actions availability close/back/filter-clear semantics Surfaces: Agent Chat History AI Presets App Launcher Browser History Browser Tabs Clipboard Current App Commands Dictation History Emoji Favorites File Search Migrate V1 Process Manager Profile Search Script Templates SDK Reference Window Switcher shared built-in helpers Concrete failure scenarios: filtered list retains an out-of-range selection. Enter executes the pre-filter row. empty state is shown while data is loading or failed. pointer first click executes rather than selects. Actions is enabled without a selected subject. count label reports dataset count as visible count or vice versa. built-in uses a third row/search/footer language rather than the shared owner. frontmost-app Paste label points at Script Kit itself. destructive built-in action lacks confirmation. an asynchronous refresh reopens or resizes a surface the user already left. For each repetitive 17-line built-in diff, verify whether it is a legitimate shared-helper adoption or merely repeated local code. Repetition is not consistency. W11 — About, confirmations, HUD, and toasts 6 paths. Trace: About back/close behavior and footer parent confirm focus and result delivery standalone confirm window ownership HUD display/dismiss lifecycle toast action callback, dismissal callback, auto-hide, and identity Concrete failure scenarios: toast action invokes the original callback twice through action plus dismissal. persistent toast auto-hides due to wrapper default. dismissible toast has no working dismissal control. action dismisses the wrong toast because IDs collide. confirmation resolves twice after keyboard plus pointer input. destructive confirm restores focus to the wrong window. About Esc closes the whole app/window rather than returning. HUD or confirm leaves footer actions enabled behind it. pending_toast_to_notification should be tested as a callback/lifecycle adapter, not accepted because it reconstructs a visually similar notification. 7. Highest-value candidate findings and conditional future pseudodiffs These are not production-edit instructions. Record them in 04-breakage-candidates.md and 09-prioritized-next-actions.md. Promote them only to the confidence established by the audit. Candidate REG-02-001 — Settings operation verb mismatch Evidence already available: descriptor operations are heterogeneous, but primary_verb is universally "Open". Trigger: select Clear Suggested, Check Permissions, Request Accessibility, or Reset Window Positions. Wrong output: footer, semantic projection, or AX projection says “Open.” Conditional future remediation: Diffdiff --git a/src/render_builtins/settings_contract.rs b/src/render_builtins/settings_contract.rs @@ - let (label, destination) = match self { + let (label, primary_verb, destination) = match self { Self::ChooseTheme => ( "Theme Designer", + "Open", SettingsDestination { ... }, ), @@ Self::ClearSuggested => ( "Clear Suggested Items", + "Clear", SettingsDestination { surface: "builtin/clear-suggested", operation: "clear", }, ), Self::CheckPermissions => ( "Check Permissions", + "Check", SettingsDestination { surface: "builtin/check-permissions", operation: "run-check", }, ), @@ Self::RequestAccessibilityPermission => ( "Request Accessibility Access", + "Request", SettingsDestination { ... }, ), Self::ResetWindowPositions => ( SETTINGS_HUB_OPTIONAL_ROW_NAME, + "Reset", SettingsDestination { ... }, ), }; @@ - primary_verb: "Open", + primary_verb, Replace every_settings_action_primary_verb_is_open with action-specific semantic assertions. Verify renderer, native footer, semantic element, AX projection, and Enter execution all consume the same descriptor. Candidate REG-02-002 — Agent Chat entry completion is count-correlated, not request-correlated Trigger: duplicate context, concurrent message mutation, delayed accepted submission, or reused thread. Wrong output: false Accepted, false context_not_staged, or false entry_timeout. Conditional future remediation request: Diffdiff --git a/src/app_impl/agent_handoff/agent_chat_entry.rs b/src/app_impl/agent_handoff/agent_chat_entry.rs @@ struct AgentChatEntryCompletionPlan { request_id: String, ... - expects_context: bool, + expected_context_semantic_ids: Vec<String>, + expected_submission_ref: Option<TurnRequestRef>, } @@ - let submitted = observed.state.message_count > plan.baseline.message_count; - let context_staged = - observed.state.context_chip_count > plan.baseline.context_count; + let submitted = plan.expected_submission_ref.as_ref().is_some_and(|expected| { + observed.state.accepted_request_refs.contains(expected) + }); + let context_staged = plan.expected_context_semantic_ids.iter().all(|expected| { + observed.state.context_semantic_ids.contains(expected) + }); This likely requires a manager-owned shared snapshot addition. Resolve its exact owner with: Bashrg -n 'struct AgentChatStateSnapshot|collect_agent_chat_state_snapshot' src crates Integration request fields: target: <resolved AgentChatStateSnapshot owner> new fields: accepted_request_refs, context_semantic_ids producer: same state source used by renderer/staging logic consumer: agent_chat_entry.rs completion resolver verification: duplicate context, concurrent mutation, delayed acceptance Do not substitute a longer timeout for correlation. Candidate REG-02-003 — Actions popup first-focus auto-close race The popup evaluates auto-close from parent focus and popup active state before its deferred focus request is installed. attachment-0001-d52ae5588439a92… Trigger: AppKit briefly reports both parent and popup inactive during initial handoff. Wrong output: popup flashes and disappears or never accepts search input. Conditional future remediation: Diffdiff --git a/src/actions/window.rs b/src/actions/window.rs @@ fn ensure_activation_subscription(...) { @@ - if should_auto_close_actions_window(parent_window_focused, actions_window_active) { + if this.did_request_focus + && should_auto_close_actions_window(parent_window_focused, actions_window_active) + { this.request_close(...); } } @@ fn render(...) { + let focus_handoff_completed_or_requested = self.did_request_focus; ... - if should_auto_close_actions_window(parent_window_focused, window_is_active) { + if focus_handoff_completed_or_requested + && should_auto_close_actions_window(parent_window_focused, window_is_active) + { self.request_close(...); } The preferred final design is an explicit lifecycle phase—Opening, FocusRequested, Active, Closing—rather than timing-dependent booleans. Do not change animation timing. Candidate GAP-02-001 — Hidden Agent Chat controls still reserve footer chrome Static evidence: predicate always returns true. First prove whether hidden controls are supposed to hide the full rail or only its buttons. If runtime shows an unintended empty band, the minimal future change is: Diff fn main_window_footer_chrome_should_render( is_agent_chat: bool, agent_chat_controls_visible: Option<bool>, ) -> bool { - let _contextual_controls_hidden = - is_agent_chat && agent_chat_controls_visible == Some(false); - true + !(is_agent_chat && agent_chat_controls_visible == Some(false)) } Before proposing this as remediation, compare resulting window geometry against the shared native-footer and glass-scroll-band contract. This is not a motion-retuning task. Candidate DEBT-02-001 — Source audits duplicate behavior or architecture that has better proof seams Future cleanup targets: remove the exact-string default-background test; retain the entity behavior test. extract clipboard_actions_dialog_config as a typed pure function and test it directly. replace “function exists” source tests with compiler-visible call sites. replace placement-helper source tests with direct geometry receipt tests. replace runtime-handle source tests with simulateGpuiEvent against the registered popup. replace parent-attachment source tests with the native lifecycle probe. retain a source audit only where no type, behavior, or runtime boundary can express the invariant. 8. Bounded verification Timeout wrapper Create this lane-local helper: Bashcat > "$LANE/run-receipt.py" <<'PY' #!/usr/bin/env python3 import os import signal import subprocess import sys import time if len(sys.argv) < 5 or sys.argv[3] != "--": raise SystemExit( "usage: run-receipt.py <timeout-seconds> <log-path> -- <command> [args...]" ) timeout = int(sys.argv[1]) log_path = sys.argv[2] command = sys.argv[4:] started = time.time() with open(log_path, "w", encoding="utf-8") as log: log.write(f"command={command!r}\n") log.write(f"timeout_seconds={timeout}\n") log.flush() process = subprocess.Popen( command, stdout=log, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, text=True, start_new_session=True, ) try: returncode = process.wait(timeout=timeout) timed_out = False except subprocess.TimeoutExpired: timed_out = True os.killpg(process.pid, signal.SIGTERM) try: returncode = process.wait(timeout=5) except subprocess.TimeoutExpired: os.killpg(process.pid, signal.SIGKILL) returncode = process.wait() elapsed = time.time() - started log.write(f"\nelapsed_seconds={elapsed:.3f}\n") log.write(f"timed_out={str(timed_out).lower()}\n") log.write(f"returncode={returncode}\n") print(f"{log_path}: returncode={returncode} timed_out={timed_out}") raise SystemExit(124 if timed_out else returncode) PY chmod +x "$LANE/run-receipt.py" Static and behavior checks Run in this order: Bashpython3 "$LANE/run-receipt.py" 1200 \ "$LANE/receipts/test-check-lib.log" -- \ ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh check --lib Expected: exit 0; no compiler errors. Bashfor FILTER in \ dialog_runtime_path_tests \ actions::window \ actions::builders::notes::tests \ quick_question_contract \ conversation_turn_render_key_tests \ prompts::chat \ settings_hub_contract_behavior \ flow_desk_create_discoverability_tests \ prompts::select \ app_impl::ui_window::tests do SAFE=$(printf '%s' "$FILTER" | tr ':/' '__') python3 "$LANE/run-receipt.py" 900 \ "$LANE/receipts/test-$SAFE.log" -- \ ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib "$FILTER" done Expected for every command: test result: ok. returncode=0 timed_out=false A filter that matches zero tests is not green. Record the zero-match result, discover the exact compiled test name with: Bash./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib -- --list \ | rg '<intended-test-or-module>' Then run it once using the corrected filter. Locked-motion anti-drift Because Actions and main-window lifecycle paths changed, run the repository-mandated anti-drift checks: Bashpython3 "$LANE/run-receipt.py" 300 \ "$LANE/receipts/test-glass-contracts.log" -- \ bun test \ scripts/devtools/glass-entry-motion-contract.test.ts \ scripts/devtools/glass-lifecycle-filmstrip.test.ts \ scripts/devtools/rapid-toggle-stress.test.ts python3 "$LANE/run-receipt.py" 900 \ "$LANE/receipts/test-glass-cargo-fixture.log" -- \ ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib \ platform::secondary_window_config_tests::glass_motion_fixture_matches_the_measured_production_calibration Expected: exit 0. Never update the fixture or thresholds to make this pass. Runtime build Bashpython3 "$LANE/run-receipt.py" 1200 \ "$LANE/receipts/build-core-audit.log" -- \ env SCRIPT_KIT_AGENT_ARTIFACT_NAME=branch-trust-core \ ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh build --bin script-kit-gpui Expected artifact: target-agent/artifacts/branch-trust-core/script-kit-gpui Runtime probe invocation contract Do not guess undocumented flags. First record the scripts’ declared environment and CLI: Bashrg -n \ 'Usage:|Bun\.argv|process\.argv|process\.env|SCRIPT_KIT_|glass-motion-calibration-theme' \ scripts/devtools/actions-entry-filmstrip.ts \ scripts/devtools/glass-lifecycle-filmstrip.ts \ scripts/devtools/rapid-toggle-stress.ts \ > "$LANE/receipts/runtime-probe-invocation-contract.txt" Read .agents/skills/script-kit-devtools/SKILL.md, then run the repository-declared invocations with: SCRIPT_KIT_TEST_STATUS=1 scripts/agentic/fixtures/glass-motion-calibration-theme.json target-agent/artifacts/branch-trust-core/script-kit-gpui Required runtime receipts: Actions open/focus/close parent window identity popup automation ID actions-dialog correct parent kind fixed-shell opening basis search input visible and focused Arrow/Enter/Escape/Cmd+K routed exactly once popup runtime handle absent after close parent focus restored Rapid toggle no orphan popup no stale singleton final open/closed state matches final input no unexpected resize/motion-contract violation Quick question start from a launcher with a real default selection invoke quick-question entry zero implicit context chips no @cmd: seed no submission then use deliberate selected-row Cmd+Enter and prove one explicit focused context Notes handoff Notes remains open main Agent Chat receives explicit @note no auto-submit existing draft and transcript survive reuse return route restores Notes Footer parity choose at least Form, Editor, Select-no-selection, Drop-no-files, Flow streaming, and Agent Chat hidden-controls states compare visible descriptor, getElements, keyboard event, and actual handler result Settings semantic projection capture footer and element/AX action for Clear, Check, Request, and Reset record whether the action says “Open” INVALID_INTERFERENCE permits one quiet-input rerun. It is neither green nor a product defect. A deterministic failure gets one diagnosis pass and one rerun without production edits. After the second result, stop and classify; manager takeover begins. 9. Screenshot requests Screenshots are optional only when the manager explicitly assigns screenshot capture. Otherwise record these requests in 07-screenshot-requests.md. Use this schema: id | state/setup | exact frame | proposed path | caption claim supported | claims not supported | paired runtime receipt Targets: S02-01-actions-root State: launcher row selected; Actions open top-center; search visible; two sections; one disabled action. Path: .artifacts/branch-trust-audit/02-core-surfaces/S02-01-actions-root.png Caption: “The branch presents contextual Actions in the launcher’s row, search, section, and shortcut language; the disabled row remains discoverable with its reason.” Does not prove: focus, shortcut execution, lifecycle, or close