Core launcher surfaces audit — patch-ready execution packet 1. Audit contract Audit main...HEAD on branch consistency/default-recommendations without modifying production source, tests, generated files, root configuration, or shared publication inputs. The lane owns exactly 128 changed paths totaling 13,122 insertions and 4,907 deletions. The supplied PackX snapshot contains only 14 selected files, so it is useful for identifying contracts and risks but cannot establish complete path coverage; the local Git diff is the authoritative evidence source. attachment-0002-3ca5760fa959a3a… attachment-0003-e173c05bcbcb763… attachment-0001-d52ae5588439a92… Apply these rules throughout: Shared components, chrome, and tokens are the owners of cross-surface consistency. Surface-local lookalikes are suspect until justified. attachment-0001-d52ae5588439a92… All Cargo invocations go through ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh. Source-reading tests are proof debt unless no higher-level invariant is possible. The preferred order is compiler/type system, lint, behavior test, runtime probe, then source audit. attachment-0001-d52ae5588439a92… Keyboard, focus, lifecycle, timing, native-window attachment, auto-submit, and asynchronous routing claims require behavior or runtime evidence. A screenshot alone cannot prove them. Do not alter locked glass-motion values, fixtures, thresholds, or expected geometry. Run the existing anti-drift checks; a failing motion check is not permission to retune. attachment-0001-d52ae5588439a92… Prior receipts, generated ledgers, comments, test names, and commit messages are claims to evaluate, not proof. 2. Verdict and confidence language Use one verdict and one confidence label on every material finding. VerdictMeaningVERIFIED_IMPROVEMENTBranch behavior is demonstrably better than main, with an appropriate proof boundary.STATIC_IMPROVEMENTDiff appears to improve structure or consistency, but user-visible behavior was not crossed.REPRODUCED_REGRESSIONConcrete input/state produces wrong behavior on the branch and does not on main, or violates an existing locked contract.PLAUSIBLE_REGRESSIONExact risky path and failure state are identified, but runtime reproduction is absent.UNPROVEN_CLAIMCode, comments, tests, or prior receipts claim behavior that available evidence does not establish.PROOF_DEBTTest or instrumentation gives false confidence, duplicates weaker proof, or checks implementation text instead of behavior.NO_MATERIAL_CHANGEDiff is plumbing, formatting, import movement, or test adaptation with no material contract change found. Confidence: R4 — Runtime-cross-boundary: built branch plus real GPUI/AppKit/process/protocol interaction, observable through repository automation, getElements, structured logs, or a native probe. R3 — Behavioral: unit or GPUI test invokes the actual descriptor, entity, handler, state machine, or dispatch seam. R2 — Structural: current diff, compiler structure, exhaustive match, typed descriptor, or source-independent static comparison. R1 — Inference: plausible from code reading but not yet falsified. R0 — Contradicted: evidence disproves the claimed improvement. A passing source-string assertion cannot raise confidence above R1. A screenshot normally caps at R2 unless paired with the runtime receipt that created the state. 3. First implementation action First read Run this before creating notes. It immediately exposes the highest-risk changed seams: Actions model/window, native footer dispatch, Agent Chat entry observation, and Settings descriptors. Bashgit diff --find-renames --function-context main...HEAD -- \ src/actions/dialog.rs \ src/actions/window.rs \ src/app_impl/ui_window.rs \ src/app_impl/agent_handoff/agent_chat_entry.rs \ src/render_builtins/settings_contract.rs \ | sed -n '1,320p' Do not start by reading prior ledgers or article drafts. First audit-artifact write Create the authoritative lane-local ownership map verbatim: BashLANE=.notes/oracle/branch-trust-audit/lanes/02-c