rsing switcher selection and return route spine integration substrate path and mutation boundaries Concrete failure scenarios: Day Page Agent action stages stale preview context after the preview closes. Agent Chat return lands on Script List rather than the original Day Page state. duplicate context is added on round trip. relative Markdown reference resolves outside the intended Brain root. day-note and normal-note identity collide. switcher selection opens Notes Window when local Day Page edit is required. stale deferred callback overwrites a newly selected day. Brain write/read claim is tested only through an in-memory helper rather than the substrate boundary. Any filesystem mutation test must use a temporary directory and must not touch the user’s actual Brain. W09 — Select, Arg, Mini, Path, and other prompts 8 paths. Trace each prompt’s: visible badge → key resolver → validation → submit callback cancel/back route → focus owner → sizing mode Concrete failure scenarios: Select with zero selections advertises enabled Run. Multiple-select prompt submits when its minimum selection contract is unmet. Drop/Path prompt submits empty data. Mini prompt consumes a key intended for its input. footer says Enter while only Cmd+Enter is handled, or the reverse. Esc cancels the script in one path but only closes UI in another. validation HUD appears but submission still proceeds. prompt mode resize uses stale item count after filter change. Focused check: Bash./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib prompts::select W10 — General built-ins 18 paths. Audit every built-in against one shared anatomy: main input/search behavior row and section owner selection reconciliation count label empty/loading/error/stale state pointer and keyboard parity native/GPUI footer parity Actions availability close/back/filter-clear semantics Surfaces: Agent Chat History AI Presets App Launcher Browser History Browser Tabs Clipboard Current App Commands Dictation History Emoji Favorites File Se