to the confidence established by the audit. Candidate REG-02-001 — Settings operation verb mismatch Evidence already available: descriptor operations are heterogeneous, but primary_verb is universally "Open". Trigger: select Clear Suggested, Check Permissions, Request Accessibility, or Reset Window Positions. Wrong output: footer, semantic projection, or AX projection says “Open.” Conditional future remediation: Diffdiff --git a/src/render_builtins/settings_contract.rs b/src/render_builtins/settings_contract.rs @@ - let (label, destination) = match self { + let (label, primary_verb, destination) = match self { Self::ChooseTheme => ( "Theme Designer", + "Open", SettingsDestination { ... }, ), @@ Self::ClearSuggested => ( "Clear Suggested Items", + "Clear", SettingsDestination { surface: "builtin/clear-suggested", operation: "clear", }, ), Self::CheckPermissions => ( "Check Permissions", + "Check", SettingsDestination { surface: "builtin/check-permissions", operation: "run-check", }, ), @@ Self::RequestAccessibilityPermission => ( "Request Accessibility Access", + "Request", SettingsDestination { ... }, ), Self::ResetWindowPositions => ( SETTINGS_HUB_OPTIONAL_ROW_NAME, + "Reset", SettingsDestination { ... }, ), }; @@ - primary_verb: "Open", + primary_verb, Replace every_settings_action_primary_verb_is_open with action-specific semantic assertions. Verify renderer, native footer, semantic element, AX projection, and Enter execution all consume the same descriptor. Candidate REG-02-002 — Agent Chat entry completion is count-correlated, not request-correlated Trigger: duplicate context, concurrent message mutation, delayed accepted submission, or reused thread. Wrong output: false Accepted, false context_not_staged, or false entry_timeout. Conditional future remediation request: Diffdiff --git a/src/app_impl/agent_handoff/agent_chat_entry.rs b/src/app_impl/agent_handoff/agent_chat_entry.rs @@ struct AgentChatEntryCompletionPlan { request_id: String, ... - expects_context: bool, + expected_context_semantic_ids: Vec<String>, + expected_submission_ref: Option<TurnRequestRef>, } @@ - let submitted = observed.state.message_count > plan.baseline.message_count; - let context_staged = - observed.state.context_chip_count > plan.baseline.context_count; + let submitted = plan.expected_submission_ref.as_ref().is_some_and(|expected| { + observed.state.accepted_request_refs.contains(expected) + }); + let context_staged = plan.expected_context_semantic_ids.iter().all(|expected| { + observed.state.context_semantic_ids.contains(expected) + }); This likely requires a manager-owned shared snapshot addition. Resolve its exact owner with: Bashrg -n 'struct AgentChatStateSnapshot|collect_agent_chat_state_snapshot' src crates Integration request fields: target: <resolved AgentChatStateSnapshot owner> new fields: accepted_request_refs, context_semantic_ids producer: same state source used by renderer/staging logic consumer: agent_chat_entry.rs completion resolver verification: duplicate context, concurrent mutation, delayed acceptance Do not substitute a longer timeout for correlation. Candidate REG-02-003 — Actions popup first-focus auto-close race The popup evaluates auto-close from parent focus and popup active state before its deferred focus request is installed. attachment-0001-d52ae5588439a92… Trigger: AppKit briefly reports both parent and popup inactive during initial handoff. Wrong output: popup flashes and disappears or never accepts search input. Conditional future remediation: Diffdiff --git a/src/actions/window.rs b/src/actions/window.rs @@ fn ensure_activation_subscription(...) { @@ - if should_auto_close_actions_window(parent_window_focused, actions_window_active) { + if this.did_request_focus + && should_auto_close_actions_window(parent_window_focused, actions_window_active) + { this.request_close(...); } } @@ fn render(...) { + let focus_handoff_completed_or_requested = self.did_request_focus; ... - if should_auto_close_actions_window(parent_window_focused, window_is_active) { + if focus_handoff_completed_or_requested + && should_auto_close_actions_window(parent_window_focused, window_is_active) + { self.request_close(...); } The preferred final design is an explicit lifecycle phase—Opening, FocusRequested, Active, Closing—rather than timing-dependent booleans. Do not change animation timing. Candidate GAP-02-001 — Hidden Agent Chat controls still reserve footer chrome Static evidence: predicate always returns true. First prove whether hidden controls are supposed to hide the full rail or only its buttons. If runtime shows an unintended empty band, the minimal future change is: Diff fn main_window_footer_chrome_should_render( is_agent_chat: bool, agent_chat_controls_visible: Option<bool>, ) -> bool { - let _contextual_controls_hidden = - is_agent_chat && agent_chat_controls_visible == Some(false); - true + !(is_agent_chat && agent_chat_controls_visible == Some(false)) } Before proposing this as remediation, compare resulting window geometry against the shared native-footer and glass-scroll-band contract. This is not a motion-retuning task. Candidate DEBT-02-001 — Source audits duplicate behavior or architecture that has better proof seams Future cleanup targets: remove the exact-string default-background test; retain the entity behavior test. extract clipboard_actions_dialog_config as a typed pure function and test it directly. replace “function exists” source tests with compiler-visible call sites. replace placement-helper source tests with direct geometry receipt tests. replace runtime-handle source tests with simulateGpuiEvent against the registered popup. replace parent-attachment source tests with the native lifecycle probe. retain a source audit only where no type, behavior, or runtime boundary can express the invariant. 8. Bounded verification Timeout wrapper Create this lane-local helper: Bashcat > "$LANE/run-receipt.py" <<'PY' #!/usr/bin/env python3 import os import signal import subprocess import sys import time if len(sys.argv) < 5 or sys.argv[3] != "--": raise SystemExit( "usage: run-receipt.py <timeout-seconds> <log-path> -- <command> [args...]" ) timeout = int(sys.argv[1]) log_path = sys.argv[2] command = sys.argv[4:] started = time.time() with open(log_path, "w", encoding="utf-8") as log: log.write(f"command={command!r}\n") log.write(f"timeout_seconds={timeout}\n") log.flush() process = subprocess.Popen( command, stdout=log, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, text=True, start_new_session=True, ) try: returncode = process.wait(timeout=timeout) timed_out = False except subprocess.TimeoutExpired: timed_out = True os.killpg(process.pid, signal.SIGTERM) try: returncode = process.wait(timeout=5) except subprocess.TimeoutExpired: os.killpg(process.pid, signal.SIGKILL) returncode = process.wait() elapsed = time.time() - started log.write(f"\nelapsed_seconds={elapsed:.3f}\n") log.write(f"timed_out={str(timed_out).lower()}\n") log.write(f"returncode={returncode}\n") print(f"{log_path}: returncode={returncode} timed_out={timed_out}") raise SystemExit(124 if timed_out else returncode) PY chmod +x "$LANE/run-receipt.py" Static and behavior checks Run in this order: Bashpython3 "$LANE/run-receipt.py" 1200 \ "$LANE/receipts/test-check-lib.log" -- \ ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh check --lib Expected: exit 0; no compiler errors. Bashfor FILTER in \ dialog_runtime_path_tests \ actions::window \ actions::builders::notes::tests \ quick_question_contract \ conversation_turn_render_key_tests \ prompts::chat \ settings_hub_contract_behavior \ flow_desk_create_discoverability_tests \ prompts::select \ app_impl::ui_window::tests do SAFE=$(printf '%s' "$FILTER" | tr ':/' '__') python3 "$LANE/run-receipt.py" 900 \ "$LANE/receipts/test-$SAFE.log" -- \ ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib "$FILTER" done Expected for every command: test result: ok. returncode=0 timed_out=false A filter that matches zero tests is not green. Record the zero-match result, discover the exact compiled test name with: Bash./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib -- --list \ | rg '<intended-test-or-module>' Then run it once using the corrected filter. Locked-motion anti-drift Because Actions and main-window lifecycle paths changed, run the repository-mandated anti-drift checks: Bashpython3 "$LANE/run-receipt.py" 300 \ "$LANE/receipts/test-glass-contracts.log" -- \ bun test \ scripts/devtools/glass-entry-motion-contract.test.ts \ scripts/devtools/glass-lifecycle-filmstrip.test.ts \ scripts/devtools/rapid-toggle-stress.test.ts python3 "$LANE/run-receipt.py" 900 \ "$LANE/receipts/test-glass-cargo-fixture.log" -- \ ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh test --lib \ platform::secondary_window_config_tests::glass_motion_fixture_matches_the_measured_production_calibration Expected: exit 0. Never update the fixture or thresholds to make this pass. Runtime build Bashpython3 "$LANE/run-receipt.py" 1200 \ "$LANE/receipts/build-core-audit.log" -- \ env SCRIPT_KIT_AGENT_ARTIFACT_NAME=branch-trust-core \ ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh build --bin script-kit-gpui Expected artifact: target-agent/artifacts/branch-trust-core/script-kit-gpui Runtime probe invocation contract Do not guess undocumented flags. First record the scripts’ declared environment and CLI: Bashrg -n \ 'Usage:|Bun\.argv|process\.argv|process\.env|SCRIPT_KIT_|glass-motion-calibration-theme' \ scripts/devtools/actions-entry-filmstrip.ts \ scripts/devtools/glass-lifecycle-filmstrip.ts \ scripts/devtools/rapid-toggle-stress.ts \ > "$LANE/receipts/runtime-probe-invocation-contract.txt" Read .agents/skills/script-kit-devtools/SKILL.md, then run the repository-declared invocations with: SCRIPT_KIT_TEST_STATUS=1 scripts/agentic/fixtures/glass-motion-calibration-theme.json target-agent/artifacts/branch-trust-core/script-kit-gpui Required runtime receipts: Actions open/focus/close parent window identity popup automation ID actions-dialog correct parent kind fixed-shell opening basis search input visible and focused